// ============================================================================
// AVIATOR V2 - DEDICATED ALWAYS-ON WORKER  [Option A, FUTURE - NOT YET ACTIVE]
// ============================================================================
// This is the higher-fidelity driver we will switch to "before production"
// (per the decision brief). It is intentionally INERT: the active driver today
// is the Supabase Edge Function in supabase/functions/game-loop/index.ts.
//
// Why upgrade later:
//   - A single long-lived process ticks every 250ms with no cold starts and no
//     minute-boundary restarts - the most robust option for real money.
//   - Runs anywhere with the service-role key (Fly.io / Railway / a VM, ~$5/mo).
//
// To activate later:
//   1. Stop the Supabase driver:   select cron.unschedule('aviator-game-loop');
//   2. Deploy this worker with env SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
//   3. Run:  deno run --allow-net --allow-env worker/game-worker.ts
//
// The DB contract is identical - both drivers only ever call public.game_tick().
// ============================================================================
